>Glynn</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Lignell</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindstrom</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exposure of perfluorinated chemicals through lactation, levels of matched human milk and serum and a temporal trend, 1996&#x02013;2004, in Sweden</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><year>2007</year><volume>115</volume><fpage>226</fpage><lpage>230</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17384769</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Calafat</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuklenyik</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Reidy</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Caudill</surname><given-names>SP</given-names></name><name><surname>Tully</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>S Needham</surname><given-names>LL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Serum concentrations of 11 polyfluoroalkyl compounds in the US population, Data from the National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey NHANES</article-title><source>Environ Sci Technol</source><year>2007</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>2237</fpage><lpage>2242</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17438769</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/es062686m</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Abbott</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolf</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmid</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Zehr</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Helfant</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Nakayama</surname><given-names>S</given-nam